<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles XII of Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1697–1718</span> · Also known as Charles XII</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles XII was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1697 to 1718 and a commander of great tactical skill. He won notable victories such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a> in 1700 but was decisively defeated by Peter I of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in 1709, after which he spent years in Ottoman exile. His death in 1718 marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> as a great power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden.jpg" alt="Charles XII of Sweden" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Hyacinthe Rigaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Copy_Charles_XII_-_Nationalmuseum_-_17886.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
